A||N||4||peterh||brake problems||||1
Z||000000||peterh||11-22-1999||08:31 AM||||The left rear caliper on my 86se does not bleed the same as the other 3 calipers. When I use the vacuum bleeder setup I bought very little fluid comes out, even when I have my wife push on brake pedal. I have taken out the bleeder valve, cleaned it with no change in results. My pedal is still feels as though it has air in system although it is better after putting in rebuilt master. The previous owner replaced rear calipers just before I purchased the car. Any body have experience with badly rebuilt calipers causing this problem?<BR>Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sage||11-22-1999||08:49 AM||||Don't know if the 86 is the same as my 84, but the 84 has rubber lines going to the caliper from the steel rear line.  These plug up on occasion.  You might try pulling it off(provided yours is not a steel line all the way to caliper) and replacing it or blowing it out with compressed air. If the calipers were replaced rather than rebuilt, there should be no problem with the caliper.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||11-22-1999||09:19 AM||||What happens with the break line is the rubber liner collapses and acts as a valve.<BR>blowing it out will not help.<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 11-22-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||11-22-1999||02:01 PM||||Are you sure that you got all the air out of the other three brake lines?  Air in one of the others could give funny results in this line.  I had that happen to me.  Everything seemed fine except I couldn't get a hard pedal.  I finally re-did all four wheels and found air in one of the others that initially seemed fine.<P>Try bleeding them all again starting with the farthest from the master cylinder and working to the closest.||||reg||1
Z||000004||peterh||11-24-1999||08:34 AM||||I finally had success with disconnecting the brake hose at the banjo fitting and pumping the pedal, fluid then came out at a good rate. Then after attaching the hose and bleeding the brakes with the pedal I was able to get better pedal. Must have been some dirt or air pocket in the hose. Thanks for the ideas.<BR>P.S. The parts store didn't list a brake blleder valve for the Fiero, so I told them to look under the Citation and it was the same bleeder.<BR>||||reg||1
